wallpaper-engine-kde-plugin (1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Scene rendering: 32-bit model indices, model-parented layer placement,
    puppet rest poses and solid-layer colors, card winding, normal transforms,
    equirect skybox pass, compose-layer camera, text effect chains and CJK
    text measurement.
  * Anti-aliasing and render-resolution settings; MSAA tiered from output size
    and pass count; exact frame pacing at the display's refresh rate.
  * Web wallpapers: one WebEngine profile per wallpaper shared across views,
    web-to-web switching rebuilds the backend, push* properties writable,
    file:// subresources allowed, bridge setters routed through a QML-only
    controller.
  * Video: failed mpv render contexts are reported; libmpv shutdown no longer
    blocks the render thread; hardware decoding gated on EGL, GL and GBM.
  * Playlists: manual navigation, merged concurrent edits, star the clicked tile.
  * Pause now stops the renderer; VT-switch handling revived; the diagnostics
    bundle scrubs the home path and is written where the user picks.
  * Stability: TextureNode redraw use-after-free, texture budget counting
    retained bytes with a runtime override, stale compiled-QML cache purged,
    hostile-input and worker-lifetime hardening, decoder leaks and load abort.
  * Fonts resolved through fontconfig; translations packaged.
  * Packaging: self-contained SRPM for Fedora, openSUSE Tumbleweed and Mageia
    from one spec; CI builds the .deb (Ubuntu LTS, Debian stable), .rpm and
    Arch package and attaches them to releases; catsout shim package and
    config migration removed.

 -- CaptSilver <591618+CaptSilver@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

wallpaper-engine-kde-plugin (1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Wallpaper playlists: editor with ordered and shuffle playback, per-monitor scope.
  * Many scene-rendering fixes: puppet rigs and attachments, scripted clocks and
    text, animation-layer blending, scene-lighting flicker, and long-runtime
    pixelation on scenes left running for hours.
  * Volumetric fog lighting for scene wallpapers.
  * Web wallpapers: sandbox file:// access, gate feature permissions, cap the HTTP cache.
  * Pause the renderer on screen lock and screensaver activation.
  * Stability: fix plasmashell crashes and data races (texture-cache use-after-free,
    shader-compile and audio-capture races, malformed-model guards).
  * Lower CPU and memory use, and faster wallpaper load, across the renderer.
  * Packaging: Arch PKGBUILD and a complete Debian build; translatable UI and
    accessibility support.

 -- CaptSilver <591618+CaptSilver@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

